# Paths excluded from the trufflehog secret scan.
#
# These are Go regexes matched against the FULL path trufflehog sees, which inside the
# hook container is /src/... .
#
# Anything naming a REPO-ROOT directory must be anchored at /src/. An unanchored fragment
# matches anywhere in the path, and `/data/` silently excluded `/src/backend/app/data/` --
# ten application source files, including the pipeline and the adapters -- from the blocking
# secret scan. The comment below said "never application source" while the pattern above it
# exempted exactly that. Anchor first, then claim it.
#
# Build outputs, caches and vendored dependencies only. Never application source.
node_modules/
\.mypy_cache/
\.ruff_cache/
\.pytest_cache/
\.git/
\.venv/
^/src/data/
^/src/frontend/dist/
^/src/frontend/coverage/
^/src/htmlcov/
package-lock\.json$
